            "notes": "In round two, you have a few options depending on how the match is playing out and what power you chose in the first round. This round is a balance of generating cash and starting to pressure the enemy [D.Va](hero_e8e1dc68-45c4-47c2-b421-95e33594e6b6), and I still tend to prioritize healing unless the other Support is also heal-focused, so I don't steal cash from them. \n\n### Chain Grasp / Ethereal Excision\n\nIf you chose [Chain Grasp](item_17b85f3e-1b10-410d-8e02-c7ff61f502a0) or [Ethereal Excision](item_a2359da3-1aa5-406f-a82f-4a0bd66266ac), focus on [Attack Speed](stat_attack_speed) and/or [Weapon Power](stat_weapon_power). Attack Speed is handy because it also buffs [Coalescence](ability_27be35ce-a74b-4ecb-abd6-297618634304), but you burn through Biotic Energy faster when healing. [Weapon Power](stat_weapon_power) buffs your healing spray and damage beam, so you might consider this if you find yourself healing a lot without access to enemies to refill your resources.\n\nIf you can afford it, [Volskaya Ordnance](item_396c0970-daa8-47e3-8049-e65f03fe5cec) is the first step to completely dominating the enemy D.Va. She almost always has >500 HP than you, so you do the full 25% extra damage on top of the 10% Attack Speed boost. If you can't buy it without selling your green items, then choose more green and blue items that boost Attack Speed or Weapon Power, and then buy it in the next round. [Shieldbuster](item_9ee1f150-537d-40b9-b975-7820fb1c6a66) is the best alternative, and if you can manage to afford both, then even better!\n\n[Aerial Distresser](item_0fcb9020-c729-49b9-b398-3223797b6204) and [Codebreaker](item_caa96c7e-655f-4d03-9bd9-0f41937fec27) are good alternatives if they have multiple flying or armored heroes. You'll get these in the later rounds anyway, so it mostly boils down to which one you want first.\n\n\n### Phantasm\n\nIf you started with [Phantasm](item_21ed9c3d-7a54-438f-9188-f21fd7a7dbfb), [Superflexor](item_580b77b4-0d63-469b-99a8-5372c55dfc1b) is one of the best (if not **the** best) early items Moira can buy if you're running a [Biotic Orb](ability_721997d0-c151-4a4c-bb11-86552b14def6) build. Your healing spray and damage beam instantly proc the maximum 25% boost to [Ability Power](stat_ability_power). All you need to do is spritz a teammate with healing (it must actually heal; it doesn't work with full-health targets) or tickle an enemy, and then [Fade](ability_438ee61f-f7ed-4321-9ca3-d3577b89ba19) near a corner/wall to drop a boosted stationary healing orb. Or, if you're harassing the enemy backline, tickling the enemy, shooting a damage orb, and then dropping one with Fade is a great pressure burst that guarantees the enemy Supports won't be focusing on their D.Va.",
