            "notes": "Round four is where we start amping up the damage pressure to [D.Va](hero_e8e1dc68-45c4-47c2-b421-95e33594e6b6).\n\n### Power\n\nUnless you chose [Ethereal Excision](item_a2359da3-1aa5-406f-a82f-4a0bd66266ac) in the first round, pick it up now. If you already have it, you can pick any of the optional powers, including [Chain Grasp](item_17b85f3e-1b10-410d-8e02-c7ff61f502a0). The rest of the powers are flexible based on your play style or how the match is progressing.\n\nI'll sometimes take [Voidhoppers](item_d4ce0c76-2500-40d6-b066-dca303be097f) if I'm staying near my team and need a Walmart [Protection Suzu](ability_e0d6579f-d70a-4a5e-a58d-aee40d00c568) to cleanse debuffs. It's handy if D.Va has [Ignition Burst](item_52bbc55a-2003-424a-99a0-a53e4941ec58) or the enemy team has other debuffs like [Dynamite](ability_036f1090-38a3-408b-a322-d0edcd17ccf7) or [Biotic Grenade](ability_06ef2826-da7f-467d-b48c-7398d5fa83fe).\n\n[Scientific Deathod](item_d61c724d-0a3e-4a28-bfb5-a7859b799981) is a good filler if you're brawling or harassing the enemy backline. It's also good in later rounds for farming your ultimate to trigger [Vanadium Injection](item_57953fbc-11ff-4e92-9928-fc59b7be668f).\n\n[Phantasm](item_21ed9c3d-7a54-438f-9188-f21fd7a7dbfb) is typically the only [Biotic Orb](ability_721997d0-c151-4a4c-bb11-86552b14def6) power I'll take. \n\n### Items\n\nIf you didn't get [Volskaya Ordnance](item_396c0970-daa8-47e3-8049-e65f03fe5cec) last round, then pick it first and fill with [Attack Speed](stat_attack_speed) and [Weapon Power](stat_weapon_power) items.\n\nIf you can afford a second epic item, choose one of these:\n\n[El-Sa'ka Supressor](item_b4298dd9-9b93-461f-a2e0-843402667100) adds a healing debuff to D.Va that she cannot block, and it's easier to maintain as her critical hitbox is center mass. \n\n[Aerial Distresser](item_0fcb9020-c729-49b9-b398-3223797b6204) against multiple fliers. \n\n[Codebreaker](item_caa96c7e-655f-4d03-9bd9-0f41937fec27) is a good choice even if D.Va is the only armored target, and you can't afford [El-Sa'ka Supressor](item_b4298dd9-9b93-461f-a2e0-843402667100) because you still get the 15% [Weapon Power](stat_weapon_power) boost for your primary and secondary fire. \n\n[Booster Jets](item_a291de85-b6d9-43cf-b5da-f3184a156f48) is a fantastic item and especially useful if you need to cover long distances or otherwise require boosted mobility. It's a staple of this build, so if you don't pick it up this round, you will later.\n\n[Weapon Jammer](item_72386db6-753e-413d-aa2a-f1389842f47f) is a bit niche, but if an enemy you're consistently targeting has boosted [Attack Speed](stat_attack_speed), then it's a solid pick.\n\n[Alternative Energy](item_c3e816b3-9c39-4528-9578-e3fa610b6cc6) is good if you're staying closer to your team or have Phantasm.\n\n[Phantasmic Flux](item_5e644a79-cf6e-4196-8d0a-232f75004643) also pairs well with Phantasm if you need the sustain. However, I don't typically take this item because I prefer going full glass cannon to maximize damage to D.Va, and use strategic cover to prevent unnecessary damage.",
