            "notes": "If you're following the main build with [Chain Grasp](item_17b85f3e-1b10-410d-8e02-c7ff61f502a0) and [Ethereal Excision](item_a2359da3-1aa5-406f-a82f-4a0bd66266ac), you should have [El-Sa'ka Supressor](item_b4298dd9-9b93-461f-a2e0-843402667100) and [Volskaya Ordnance](item_396c0970-daa8-47e3-8049-e65f03fe5cec). If you can afford a third epic, choose [Codebreaker](item_caa96c7e-655f-4d03-9bd9-0f41937fec27) and then fill with [Weapon Power](stat_weapon_power) and [Attack Speed](stat_attack_speed) items.\n\nIf you have [Phantasm](item_21ed9c3d-7a54-438f-9188-f21fd7a7dbfb) and don't have [Ethereal Excision](item_a2359da3-1aa5-406f-a82f-4a0bd66266ac), you can sub [Phantasmic Flux](item_5e644a79-cf6e-4196-8d0a-232f75004643) or [Superflexor](item_580b77b4-0d63-469b-99a8-5372c55dfc1b) for [El-Sa'ka Supressor](item_b4298dd9-9b93-461f-a2e0-843402667100). That said, you should have chosen Ethereal Excision in the first or third round, so try avoiding this path.\n\nIf you find that your team absolutely cannot exist without you healing them or you can manage both simultaneously, [Amari's Antidote](item_67e0b1c5-3bcb-4ab5-b818-5082e5706124) is a good pick.",
