        {
            "id": "18971e33-d535-40ad-8f7d-d32cc60f9b35",
            "build_id": "2b3d6c75-6b3d-455c-acc0-5b80cc83a77a",
            "round_number": 5,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-09-19T19:34:13.244576+00:00",
            "notes": "By round five, the core build should be complete. Since [Ethereal Excision](item_a2359da3-1aa5-406f-a82f-4a0bd66266ac) is the only power I'd call required, you can pick whatever best fits you, teams, map, situation, etc. If the enemy [D.Va](hero_e8e1dc68-45c4-47c2-b421-95e33594e6b6) has you figured out and has [Facetanking](item_f8af63d1-1fd4-4758-86ce-96f1ef7ea1ea) and [Plot Armor](item_d1427316-79d1-43a7-a608-67beb1595131), it might be a good time to flex into a different build or style, but it's not necessary. For example, if I notice she's using [Defense Matrix](ability_88831f83-b0fd-434b-92f5-afdc1d809da2) in my direction a lot and has that power/item combo, I'll change my angle so she has to look at me and not my team. The only reason to be looking at her head-on is for the critical damage healing debuff, so you can still melt her really well when she's not facing you. \n\nIf she starts avoiding you and you can't chase her around, go on an adventure and wreck her team. Most of the items and powers work just as well against other heroes, so shifting your focus to the rest of her team can be just as devastating to them.\n\nIf you're flush with cash, consider adding in [Eye of the Spider](item_bbaf01d7-340d-4199-b738-86a98d68fe9b).",
